All calculations must use fixed-precision decimal
arithmetic.

Never use floating-point numbers for authoritative
money or precious-metal calculations.

Keep source measurements and units.

Store:

Calculated purity
Declared purity
Assay results
Recovery estimates

as separate values where appropriate.

Do not hide unexplained weight differences.

Implement independent reconciliation reports.

Metal balances must be traceable to
source transactions.

Create automated invariants that identify
unexplained differences.

Never silently change balances to make
a report appear correct.


