34. CRITICAL TRANSACTION INVARIANTS
==================================================

The following invariants are mandatory.

INVARIANT 1:
One unique available article cannot be sold
by two counters simultaneously.

INVARIANT 2:
Every posted financial journal must balance.

INVARIANT 3:
A sale cannot silently update stock without
its corresponding financial posting.

INVARIANT 4:
A payment webhook replay cannot duplicate
money received.

INVARIANT 5:
Historical invoices must retain original
calculation parameters.

INVARIANT 6:
Customer-owned repair inventory must remain
separate from merchant-owned inventory.

INVARIANT 7:
A stock transfer must not create extra
physical quantity.

INVARIANT 8:
A return must reference an eligible original
transaction.

INVARIANT 9:
A refunded transaction must not be refunded
twice through retry or concurrency.

INVARIANT 10:
A closed financial period cannot be silently
modified.

INVARIANT 11:
A tenant cannot access another tenant's data.

INVARIANT 12:
Every metal adjustment must have an authorized,
traceable reason.

INVARIANT 13:
Repeated imports cannot duplicate opening stock
or balances.

INVARIANT 14:
Invoice reprinting cannot create new sales.

INVARIANT 15:
External notification failures cannot reverse
an otherwise valid posted transaction.

Build automated tests for all invariants.


